<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart - Feb 7-9.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart - Feb 7-9.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the February 7-9 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p> 1. Star Wars		  $24,277,091	 $ 70,758,529</p>
<p> 2. Dante's Peak	     $18,479,435	 $  ----</p>
<p> 3. The Beautician</p>
<p>    and the Beast	   $ 4,080,822	  $  ----</p>
<p> 4. Jerry Maguire	    $ 3,580,033	 $121,282,251</p>
<p> 5. Scream		     $ 3,563,218	 $ 75,008,414</p>
<p> 6. Evita			$ 3,001,066	 $ 40,993,867</p>
<p> 7. Metro			$ 2,492,775	 $ 28,412,067</p>
<p> 8. The English Patient    $ 2,237,749	 $ 42,013,561</p>
<p> 9. Beverly Hills Ninja    $ 2,014,802	 $ 27,050,978</p>
<p> 10 Michael		    $ 1,942,705	 $ 83,056,061</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Star Wars&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp.. &quot;Dante's Peak&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.. &quot;The Beautician and the Beast&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.. &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; and &quot;Beverly Hills Ninja&quot; are released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Scream&quot; and &quot;The English Patient&quot; are released by Miramax Films, a unit of Walt Disney Co.. &quot;Metro&quot; and &quot;Evita&quot; are released by Disney. &quot;Michael&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
